[stderr] ## Mechanical release checks
[stderr] 
[stderr] The editorial validator must derive, rather than trust, the following report
[stderr] from published card records and their provenance/review records:
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Check | Required result |
[stderr] | --- | --- |
[stderr] | ID/boundary | Exactly 48 unique IDs, exactly `QB-A-01…48`, exactly four named batches of 12; no extra QB-A card. |
[stderr] | Category | World tournament history, domestic league moments, club/manager/identity, and players/records each equal 12. |
[stderr] | Difficulty | Each category contains exactly four band-1, four band-2, and four band-3 cards. |
[stderr] | Format | Each named batch contains exactly three FO, three TF, three OP, and three TA cards; therefore the release has 12 of each format. |
[stderr] | Competition | No `competitionScopes` value appears on more than six cards: the declared maximums are FIFA World Cup 6, UEFA European Championship 3, Copa América 3, AFC Asian Cup 3, Premier League 6, LALIGA 4, Serie A 6, UEFA Champions League 6, and Ballon d'Or 2. |
[stderr] | Club | No `clubIds` value appears on more than four cards: Liverpool, Barcelona, and AC Milan each appear four times; other cards have no club quota participant. |
[stderr] | Eligibility | Every card is `published`, has all grammar fields, a resolvable provenance record with a checked date, no unresolved conflict, two distinct accepted reviews of its current revision, and no withdrawal. |
[stderr] | Originality/accessibility | Every card has accepted originality and accessibility/copy review findings, required text equivalents, and no player-facing copied/source text. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] The sample inventory intentionally remains `draft` until per-card research and
[stderr] review are completed. Thus it is bounded and independently auditable now, while
[stderr] the validator will correctly reject it as a shippable package until its
[stderr] provenance and both reviews are supplied.
[stderr] ### design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md
[stderr] # Round lifecycle bible
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Scope:** accepted design evidence for `GAME-005`, `GAME-006`, `GPI-008`, and
[stderr] `GPI-009`. This defines a future-core contract and fixtures, not production
[stderr] content or an implementation. All content IDs refer to the frozen package held
[stderr] by the run; no network response, wall clock, UI ordering, or random source can
[stderr] alter a fixture result.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## GPI-008 — First Whistle tutorial
[stderr] 
[stderr] `First Whistle` is a fixed five-card, non-timed onboarding round. It is
[stderr] available from a new local profile when the installed tutorial package is
[stderr] present, including offline. It does not need sign-in, a purchase, notifications,
[stderr] or a remote service. Each card has the indicated one purpose; its final
[stderr] published wording, answer IDs, provenance, and two reviews are governed by the
[stderr] question-card and adjudication bibles before it may ship.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Position / ID | Fixed format | Instructional purpose | Required resolution and next state |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | 1 / `TUT-01` | four-option select | Read the prompt, choose one labelled option, and confirm. | Accepted or rejected select submission resolves the attempt, exposes text feedback, and opens `TUT-02`. |
[stderr] | 2 / `TUT-02` | short typed answer | Enter a short answer and confirm; only configured canonical text/aliases are accepted. | A typed submission resolves through GAME-003 normalisation, shows canonical answer/explanation if rejected, and opens `TUT-03`. |
[stderr] | 3 / `TUT-03` | true/false | Recognise that feedback says whether the resolved answer was accepted. | Submission resolves once; feedback is available in text plus non-colour state, then opens `TUT-04`. |
[stderr] | 4 / `TUT-04` | ordered pair | Inspect the explanation after resolving an answer. | Submission resolves once; explanation is available before continue, then opens `TUT-05`. |
[stderr] | 5 / `TUT-05` | four-option select | Pause deliberately, confirm that the current safe state is saved, then resume and finish. | Explicit pause commits a snapshot after the unresolved card is displayed; resume restores `TUT-05`; resolved completion commits result and `first_whistle_complete`. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] The tutorial's card sequence is exactly `[TUT-01, TUT-02, TUT-03, TUT-04,
[stderr] TUT-05]`; it has no selection seed, repeat filter, timer, skip, or reordering.
[stderr] The tutorial selection never silently substitutes an unavailable card. If its
[stderr] fixed package is unavailable or invalid, start is blocked with a plain-language
[stderr] retry/return-home state.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Tutorial deterministic fixtures
[stderr] 
[stderr] Fixture input includes a frozen `tutorial-v1` package containing the five IDs,
[stderr] a new local profile, and the stated actions. `resolve` means the matching
[stderr] GAME-003 fixture supplies an immutable accepted/rejected attempt; the
[stderr] particular football fact is deliberately not duplicated here.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Input / action | Expected deterministic state, record, and visible outcome |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `TUT-FX-01` | Start `tutorial-v1`; resolve `TUT-01`; continue. | Active card changes `TUT-01 → TUT-02`; one immutable TUT-01 attempt exists; no timer state is created. |
[stderr] | `TUT-FX-02` | From TUT-02 submit a configured typed alias, resolve, continue. | `TUT-02 → TUT-03`; outcome is the configured GAME-003 alias result and is not recomputed on continue. |
[stderr] | `TUT-FX-03` | From TUT-03 submit an incorrect valid true/false value, resolve, continue. | `TUT-03 → TUT-04`; rejected text/non-colour feedback and canonical answer/explanation are recorded before continue. |
[stderr] | `TUT-FX-04` | From TUT-04 submit its configured ordered pair, resolve, inspect explanation, continue. | `TUT-04 → TUT-05`; explanation availability is recorded; inspection does not change score, streak, or card position. |
[stderr] | `TUT-FX-05` | Display TUT-05; `Pause`; restart; `Resume`; resolve; complete. | Pause snapshot has `activeCardId=TUT-05`, no unresolved answer, package `tutorial-v1`; restart restores that card; completion creates exactly one `first_whistle_complete` milestone and an immutable result. |
[stderr] | `TUT-FX-06` | Repeat the completion command in TUT-FX-05 with the same completed-run ID and interaction ID. | Return the recorded completion/result; no second milestone, history entry, or score event is added. |
[stderr] | `TUT-FX-07` | Start tutorial while offline with `tutorial-v1` cached; pause at TUT-05; restart while still offline. | Start, snapshot read, and resume succeed using cached package only; no network request is required. |
[stderr] | `TUT-FX-08` | Start tutorial with no compatible cached tutorial package. | No run is created; show initial-content-required/retry/return-home state. It must not offer a substituted or partial tutorial. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## GPI-009 — Mixed Fixture selection
[stderr] 
[stderr] `Mixed Fixture` starts with `(catalogueSnapshotId, selectionSeed, theme,
[stderr] repeatLedger, timerMode)`. `theme` is either one selected category or
[stderr] `kickoff_mix`; requested count is always ten. The selection first applies the
[stderr] GAME-004 frozen-catalogue, publication, withdrawal, filter, anti-repeat, and
[stderr] SHA-256 ordering policy. It then constructs the longest deterministic prefix
[stderr] whose next card would not create a run of three equal `format` or three equal
[stderr] `difficulty`. At each position, choose the first ranked candidate that keeps
[stderr] both run lengths at two or fewer. If none does, choose the first ranked
[stderr] candidate and append a variety-shortage record. This tie-free rule makes
[stderr] selection reproducible and never rerolls.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The saved selection contains selected card IDs/revisions, their frozen package
[stderr] and rule versions, rank inputs, `selectionSeed`, timer mode, and both shortage
[stderr] records. A shortage is displayed before start with the plain-language key
[stderr] `selection_shortage_reuse_disclosed` (reuse/unfilled) and/or
[stderr] `selection_shortage_variety_disclosed` (three-in-a-row unavoidable). A category
[stderr] with no eligible cards does not create a run; it shows unavailable-category and
[stderr] offers another eligible theme.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Seeded Mixed Fixture fixtures
[stderr] 
[stderr] In these fixtures `ranked` is the ascending SHA-256 ordering already calculated
[stderr] from the stated frozen snapshot and seed under GAME-004. Each token is
[stderr] `ID:format:difficulty`; all candidates are published, in theme, and eligible
[stderr] after the repeat policy unless a shortage field says otherwise.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Snapshot / seed / ranked candidates | Expected selected IDs and records |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `MIX-FX-01` | `MF-1` / `north`; `A:S:1,B:T:2,C:O:3,D:S:2,E:T:1,F:O:2,G:S:3,H:T:1,I:O:2,J:S:1,K:T:3,L:O:1` | `A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J`; 10 fresh cards, no reuse/unfilled/variety shortage; every adjacent triple differs in both format and difficulty. |
[stderr] | `MIX-FX-02` | `MF-2` / `west`; `A:S:1,B:S:2,C:S:3,D:T:1,E:O:2,F:T:3,G:O:1,H:S:2,I:T:1,J:O:3` | `A,B,D,C,E,F,G,H,I,J`; C moves after D because `A,B,C` would be three selects; no shortage. |
[stderr] | `MIX-FX-03` | `MF-3` / `east`; `A:S:1,B:T:1,C:O:1,D:S:2,E:T:2,F:O:2,G:S:3,H:T:3,I:O:3,J:S:1` | `A,B,D,C,E,F,G,H,I,J`; D moves before C because the first three ranked cards share difficulty 1; no shortage. |
[stderr] | `MIX-FX-04` | `MF-4` / `south`; `A:S:1,B:S:2,C:S:3,D:S:1,E:S:2,F:S:3,G:S:1,H:S:2,I:S:3,J:S:1` | `A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J`; formats have no alternative, so record format variety shortages at positions 3–10 with `selection_shortage_variety_disclosed` before start. |
[stderr] | `MIX-FX-05` | `MF-5` / `cup`; fresh ranked `A:S:1,B:T:2,C:O:3,D:S:2,E:T:1,F:O:2,G:S:3,H:T:2`, then reused ranked `I:O:3,J:S:1`; requested 10 | Select A–H then I,J; record reused IDs I,J and `selection_shortage_reuse_disclosed`; variety rule is still evaluated over the final order. |
[stderr] | `MIX-FX-06` | `MF-6` / `cup`; seven eligible ranked `A:S:1,B:T:2,C:O:3,D:S:2,E:T:1,F:O:2,G:S:3`; requested 10 | Select A–G only; record `requestedCount=10`, `eligibleAvailable=7`, `unfilledCount=3`, and `selection_shortage_reuse_disclosed`; do not pad with unpublished, withdrawn, or invented cards. |
[stderr] | `MIX-FX-07` | `MF-7` / `empty-theme`; no eligible candidates | No run/snapshot; show unavailable-category and eligible-theme choice. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Optional timer and round lifecycle
[stderr] 
[stderr] Timer is an accessibility-neutral optional display mode: `off` is the default
[stderr] and tutorial always forces `off`. Starting a standard round freezes the chosen
[stderr] mode. `on` records elapsed active seconds only; it does not change selection,
[stderr] adjudication, score, streak, or availability. Pause, background interruption,
[stderr] and recovery stop elapsed time. A timeout can be emitted only for an explicitly
[stderr] enabled timer according to the separately implemented GAME-007 scoring rule.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Transition | Preconditions | Required result |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `home → selecting_theme` | Compatible cached standard package. | Show themes and timer choice defaulted to off. |
[stderr] | `selecting_theme → ready` | Valid theme and deterministic selection. | Show selected count and any shortage disclosure before start. |
[stderr] | `ready → active(card 1)` | Start accepted. | Freeze cards/revisions/package/rules/seed/timer mode into run snapshot. |
[stderr] | `active(card n) → feedback(card n)` | One valid submission or enabled-timer timeout. | Create one immutable attempt; prevent a duplicate submission from creating another. |
[stderr] | `feedback(card n) → active(card n+1)` | Continue and `n < cardCount`. | Save resolved safe boundary before showing the next unresolved card. |
[stderr] | `feedback(last) → results` | Continue after final resolution. | Commit result once; reopening is idempotent. |
[stderr] | `active or feedback → paused` | Explicit pause, background/interruption, or app shutdown at safe boundary. | Persist current safe snapshot; timer stops; no answer is inferred or submitted. |
[stderr] | `paused → active or feedback` | Resume compatible confirmed snapshot. | Restore exact card, resolved-feedback state if any, selection and timer mode; content cannot switch mid-round. |
[stderr] | `paused → recovery` | Draft corrupt/incompatible or write interrupted. | Preserve last confirmed snapshot and offer resume it, discard draft, or return home; never overwrite silently. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Lifecycle deterministic fixtures
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Input / action | Expected result |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-01` | Start `MIX-FX-01` with no timer choice. | Run records `timerMode=off`; no timeout is schedulable or shown. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-02` | Start `MIX-FX-01` with timer on; 12 active seconds; pause; wait 30 seconds; resume. | Elapsed value is 12 on pause and resume; 30 paused seconds are excluded. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-03` | Resolve card 1, then retry its submit command with same interaction ID. | One attempt/score event exists and active card is card 2 exactly once. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-04` | On active card 4, app backgrounds; process terminates; restart. | Restore the last confirmed active-card-4 snapshot with no inferred answer; timer remains stopped until resumed. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-05` | Resolve card 4, then storage write fails before promotion. | Keep prior confirmed snapshot, surface retry/continue-without-saving, and do not claim card 4 was saved. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-06` | A compatible package update arrives during an active `MF-1` run. | Current run continues on its frozen package; update stages for between rounds only. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-07` | Restart with corrupt draft but valid confirmed card-4 snapshot. | Quarantine draft and offer the confirmed snapshot or discard; do not silently start a different selection. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-08` | Complete and reopen a standard result with the same completed-run ID. | Return the stored result; no duplicate aggregate history, score, or milestone is created. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-09` | From home with compatible cached package, choose the `cup` theme and leave timer off. | Traverse `home → selecting_theme → ready`; ready state shows the deterministic `MIX-FX-05` IDs/count and its reuse disclosure before start. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-10` | Start the ready state in LIFE-FX-09. | Traverse `ready → active(card 1)` and commit frozen IDs/revisions, `MF-5`, selection seed, rule/package versions, and `timerMode=off`. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-11` | Resolve and continue cards 1–9 of LIFE-FX-01, then resolve and continue card 10. | Each of the first nine continuations traverses `feedback(card n) → active(card n+1)` after a safe save; the tenth traverses `feedback(last) → results` once. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-12` | Pause from feedback after resolving card 4, restart, and resume. | Traverse `feedback → paused → feedback`; card-4 feedback, explanation availability, and frozen selection are restored without a second attempt. |
[stderr] | `LIFE-FX-13` | Detect an incompatible/corrupt draft while paused and choose the recovery route. | Traverse `paused → recovery`; retain the confirmed snapshot and show resume-confirmed/discard-draft/return-home choices. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Accessibility and release boundary
[stderr] 
[stderr] Every transition has a visible text state and an equivalent touch, pointer,
[stderr] keyboard, and gamepad action. Focus is visible; pause/resume, timer state,
[stderr] shortage disclosure, save success/failure, selected answer, correct/incorrect,
[stderr] and explanation are never communicated by colour, animation, or audio alone.
[stderr] Timer on/off is labelled, reversible before start, and compatible with reduced
[stderr] motion and muted/captioned feedback. There is no ranked, daily, live, event,
[stderr] account-only, or target-exclusive round mode in this scope.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Release validation requires exactly `TUT-FX-01`–`TUT-FX-08`,
[stderr] `MIX-FX-01`–`MIX-FX-07`, and `LIFE-FX-01`–`LIFE-FX-13`, with each named tutorial
[stderr] card and every lifecycle transition covered above. Published card facts and
[stderr] answer rules remain subject to the editorial/provenance validation contracts.
[stderr] ### design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md
[stderr] # Score, streak, and results bible
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Scope:** accepted design evidence for `GAME-007`, `GAME-008`, `GPI-010`, and
[stderr] `GPI-011`. This is a deterministic future-core contract, not implementation or
[stderr] production content. It consumes immutable `GAME-003` adjudication outcomes and
[stderr] the frozen run/card sequence from `GPI-009`. A run ID, attempt ID, interaction
[stderr] ID, and completion ID are stable UUID-like opaque values; retries reuse the
[stderr] relevant ID and never derive a second event from timing, UI order, or a network
[stderr] response.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## GPI-010 — score and streak contract
[stderr] 
[stderr] An attempt first resolves exactly once to one of `correct`, `wrong`, `blank`,
[stderr] `timeout`, or `abandoned`. `blank` is an explicit confirm with no answer;
[stderr] `timeout` may occur only when the player explicitly chose the enabled timer
[stderr] mode; and `abandoned` records a deliberate abandon command, never an inferred
[stderr] answer from pause, backgrounding, crash, or loss of focus. Pausing and recovery
[stderr] therefore preserve the unresolved attempt and are not scoring outcomes.
[stderr] 
[stderr] `scoreBefore`, `streakBefore`, `scoreDelta`, `streakAfter`, and `scoreAfter`
[stderr] are written to the immutable score event when the attempt resolves. The event
[stderr] is the source of a reopened feedback or result surface; the score is never
[stderr] recomputed from changed content or presentation settings.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Resolved outcome | Score delta | Streak after resolution | Feedback state | Continue/recovery rule |
[stderr] | --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `correct`, streak before 0–1 | +100 | streak before + 1 | `correct_base` | Explanation and continue are available. |
[stderr] | `correct`, streak before 2 | +125 | 3 | `correct_streak` | First streak bonus is +25; announce the three-in-a-row state. |
[stderr] | `correct`, streak before 3 | +150 | 4 | `correct_streak` | Bonus rises to +50. |
[stderr] | `correct`, streak before 4 | +175 | 5 | `correct_streak` | Bonus rises to +75. |
[stderr] | `correct`, streak before 5 | +200 | 6 | `correct_streak_cap` | The bonus reaches its +100 cap. |
[stderr] | `correct`, streak before 6 or more | +200 | streak before + 1 | `correct_streak_cap` | Bonus stays capped at +100; no further increase. |
[stderr] | `wrong` | +0 | 0 | `incorrect` | Show canonical answer/explanation; player may continue or pause. |
[stderr] | `blank` | +0 | 0 | `blank` | Explain that no answer was submitted; player may continue or pause. |
[stderr] | `timeout` | +0 | 0 | `timeout` | Only valid with frozen `timerMode=on`; show the answer/explanation and continue/pause controls. |
[stderr] | `abandoned` | +0 | 0 | `abandoned` | End this run recoverably; preserve its partial result and offer resume/replay/theme/exit as applicable. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] The active streak has no maximum. After a correct resolution, `bonus =
[stderr] min(100, max(0, 25 × (streakAfter - 2)))`; thus the first three-correct streak
[stderr] adds +25 and every later correct adds another +25 until the +100 cap. A correct
[stderr] answer is worth at most 200 points. `scoreAfter = scoreBefore + scoreDelta`;
[stderr] score is a non-negative monotonic total. `bestActiveSessionStreak` is the
[stderr] maximum resolved correct streak in this run and never falls when the active
[stderr] streak resets. A retry is a new `runId`; it retains aggregate history but never
[stderr] overwrites the prior run's attempts or score events.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Equivalent feedback requirements
[stderr] 
[stderr] Each feedback state exposes the same outcome in four independently useful
[stderr] forms. Assets and cues may decorate these forms but cannot be the only carrier
[stderr] of meaning.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | State | Required text and semantic label | Required non-colour visual | Caption/mute audio equivalent | Reduced-motion behaviour |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `correct_base` | “Correct. +100 points. Streak: N.” | Success icon/pattern plus labelled score panel. | If the correct cue plays, caption `Correct; 100 points; streak N`; mute leaves all text visible. | Static labelled state; no animation required. |
[stderr] | `correct_streak` | “Correct. +[100 + bonus] points. Streak: N. Streak bonus +[25/50/75].” | Success icon/pattern plus a labelled streak marker. | Caption names correct result, points, streak, and bonus; mute changes no score information. | Replace celebration movement with static marker. |
[stderr] | `correct_streak_cap` | “Correct. +200 points. Streak: N. Bonus capped at +100.” | Success icon/pattern plus labelled cap marker. | Caption names capped bonus and points; mute changes no score information. | Static cap marker; no pulsing or forced animation. |
[stderr] | `incorrect`, `blank`, `timeout` | Outcome name, “+0 points”, “Streak reset”, canonical answer, and explanation. | Distinct labelled error/empty/time pattern; not red or animation alone. | Caption names outcome, zero points, reset, answer, and explanation availability; mute leaves this text visible. | Static feedback and controls. |
[stderr] | `abandoned` | “Round ended. No points lost. Streak reset.” plus the recovery/next action. | Distinct labelled exit/interrupted pattern. | Caption names end state and next action; mute leaves this text visible. | Static end state and focusable action. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] Screen-reader semantics announce the same text once per resolved attempt. Focus
[stderr] moves to the feedback heading, not an animation. All feedback includes visible
[stderr] continue, pause, and where relevant replay/theme/exit actions with equivalent
[stderr] touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad operation.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Score and feedback edge fixtures
[stderr] 
[stderr] All fixtures start from a frozen `Mixed Fixture` run unless stated otherwise.
[stderr] Each `resolve` command has a unique interaction ID, and a repeated command uses
[stderr] the same one.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Input / action | Expected immutable record and visible outcome |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-01` | Correct with score 0, streak 0. | One event: `+100`, streak 1, score 100, `correct_base`; text/non-colour/caption equivalents agree. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-02` | From streak 1, correct. | One event: `+100`, streak 2, score rises by 100; no bonus message. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-03` | From score 200, streak 2, correct. | One event: `+125`, streak 3, score 325, `correct_streak`; text and caption name +25 bonus. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-04` | From score 325, streak 3, correct. | One event: `+150`, streak 4, score 475; bonus rises to +50. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-05` | From score 475, streak 4, correct. | One event: `+175`, streak 5, score 650; feedback names the +75 bonus. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-06` | From score 650, streak 5, correct; then from streak 6, correct again. | The first event is `+200`, streak 6, score 850, `correct_streak_cap`; the second is `+200`, streak 7, score 1050, proving the +100 cap does not rise. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-07` | From score 1050, streak 7, resolve `wrong`. | One zero-point event, active streak 0, score remains 1050, best streak remains 7; answer/explanation and static non-colour feedback are available. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-08` | From score 1050, streak 4, explicitly submit blank. | One zero-point `blank` event, active streak 0, score remains 1050; no answer is guessed and continue/pause remain available. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-09` | With frozen `timerMode=on`, from score 1050, streak 3, let the enabled timer expire. | One zero-point `timeout` event, active streak 0, score remains 1050; answer/explanation and static timeout feedback are available. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-10` | With frozen `timerMode=off`, wait beyond the configured duration. | No timeout, attempt, score event, or streak reset is created; card remains unresolved. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-11` | From score 450, streak 4, choose abandon; reopen the partial result. | One zero-point `abandoned` event/reset and one partial result; score remains 450, no completion milestone is awarded, and reopening returns that record. |
[stderr] | `SCORE-FX-12` | Resolve a correct answer, then resend the same resolve command/interaction ID; enable mute and reduced motion before reopening feedback. | Exactly one attempt and score event exist; reopened feedback is static and text/non-colour equivalent remains complete with no audio required. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## GPI-011 — results and local milestone contract
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Result states
[stderr] 
[stderr] | State | Trigger and required stored fields | Available actions | Milestone effect |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `in_progress` | A run with frozen content/rules, score events, and a current safe boundary. | Resume, pause, abandon, return home only through a safe boundary. | None. |
[stderr] | `completed_result` | Last resolved attempt is continued; immutable `ResultSummary` has `runId`, `completionId`, answered, correct, score, best active-session streak, category, outcome counts, and action labels. | Replay (new run), choose theme, exit, reopen result. | Tutorial only: request `first_whistle_complete`. |
[stderr] | `abandoned_result` | Explicit abandon; immutable partial summary has the same fields plus `endedReason=abandoned`. | Resume only if a compatible safe snapshot precedes abandonment; otherwise replay, choose theme, exit, reopen result. | None. |
[stderr] | `recovery` | Draft is corrupt/incompatible or a write was interrupted; last confirmed snapshot is retained. | Resume confirmed, discard draft, return home. | None until a real completion commits. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] `answered` counts immutable resolved attempts. `correct` counts only `correct`.
[stderr] `score` and `bestActiveSessionStreak` copy the committed score-event ledger.
[stderr] The summary identifies the frozen category, not a current theme label that may
[stderr] change. It displays score, answered/correct, best active-session streak,
[stderr] category, and labelled replay/choose-theme/exit actions. It has no rank, RPG
[stderr] level, loot, social comparison, or account dependency.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Completion and milestone idempotence
[stderr] 
[stderr] Completion is a single atomic logical operation keyed by `(runId, completionId)`:
[stderr] write/retrieve the immutable `ResultSummary`, write/retrieve its aggregate
[stderr] history entry, and, only for a completed tutorial, write/retrieve
[stderr] `first_whistle_complete`. A duplicate command with that key returns the stored
[stderr] objects unchanged. A completion command for a different run ID is not a retry;
[stderr] it may create a distinct result and, for another tutorial run, returns the
[stderr] existing milestone rather than a second one.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The `first_whistle_complete` milestone is a presence state keyed to the local
[stderr] profile, not a counter. Its first stored value includes the source tutorial
[stderr] run/completion ID and completion timestamp. Later tutorial completions may add
[stderr] their own immutable history/result once, but cannot replace those provenance
[stderr] fields or create another milestone. Reopen, restart, failed UI acknowledgement,
[stderr] and recovery replay are reads unless they initiate a new run.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Result and lifecycle fixtures
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Input / action | Expected deterministic state and idempotence result |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `RESULT-FX-01` | Complete a standard 10-card run, then reopen using its run/completion ID. | One `completed_result`, history entry, and score ledger are stored; reopen returns them without any duplicate completion or milestone. |
[stderr] | `RESULT-FX-02` | Complete `tutorial-v1` TUT-05, then repeat completion after restart with the same IDs. | Exactly one result/history entry and one profile `first_whistle_complete` presence state; retry returns both unchanged. |
[stderr] | `RESULT-FX-03` | Explicitly abandon after card 4, restart, and open its result. | One `abandoned_result`, zero-point abandon event, and no completion milestone; partial score/history is recoverable and no attempt is inferred for card 5. |
[stderr] | `RESULT-FX-04` | Pause at an unresolved card, background/terminate, restart, then resume and complete. | Restore the confirmed unresolved card with no abandon/blank/timeout event; later completion creates one result and eligible tutorial milestone only once. |
[stderr] | `RESULT-FX-05` | On final-card completion, result write is interrupted; restart with a valid prior confirmed snapshot and corrupt draft. | Enter `recovery`, retain snapshot, offer resume-confirmed/discard-draft/return-home; no result or milestone is claimed until a successful completion commits. |
[stderr] | `RESULT-FX-06` | Complete a tutorial, confirm deletion of local history/profile/snapshots, restart, and complete a new tutorial run. | Deletion returns to first launch and removes old local records only after confirmation; the new profile/run can create one new result and one new milestone, with no duplicate residual completion. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Release boundary
[stderr] 
[stderr] Release validation requires `SCORE-FX-01`–`SCORE-FX-12` and
[stderr] `RESULT-FX-01`–`RESULT-FX-06`: exactly 18 fixtures. Wrong, blank, enabled
[stderr] timeout, and explicit abandon are all recoverable outcomes with a monotonic
[stderr] score and no duplicate completion. Pause, interruption, and recovery are not
[stderr] substitutes for those outcomes and cannot silently manufacture an attempt.
