+  card-level records for the existing `QB-A-01`–`QB-A-48`, grouped into the
+  existing four named 12-card batches. Each record must identify the current
+  revision, original-expression/non-copying decision, durable permitted source
+  locator and checked date for every factual assertion, conflict/correction
+  state, factual/rights review, accessibility/copy review, independent second
+  review, and resulting lifecycle status.
+- Update `design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md` only as
+  needed to point to the register and replace the explicitly pending catalogue
+  state after all 48 records qualify. Preserve its existing quotas, IDs, and
+  source policy.
+
+The successor must leave rejected, unresolved, withdrawn, conflicted, or
+incompletely reviewed cards ineligible and state the exact reason. It must not
+set `planning/game-design-manifest.json` to accepted. A later `GQ` audit is the
+only task allowed to run the dedicated completion check, update canonical
+bible/inventory records, and accept that manifest.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- All 48 existing QB-A card revisions have independently inspectable
+  original-expression, provenance, and two-distinct-review evidence, or every
+  remaining ineligible card has its exact pending or blocked reason retained.
+- The four existing batches remain finite at 12 cards each and no unreviewed
+  record can enter selection.
