criteria\n\n- No more than five G tasks are created and it declares `design_authoring_batch: GB0003`.\n### game-design-runbooks/G0001.md\n---\ntask_id: G0001\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: GB0001\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005\ntitle: Define original football question-card and catalogue bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0001\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted detailed evidence for GAME-001\u2013002/GPI-001\u2013005: card grammar, answer/explanation/provenance/accessibility fields, and four named 12-card QB-A batches with exact format/difficulty/topic quotas and two-review workflow.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md`: original question-card grammar and four named QB-A editorial batches, including permitted sources, factual and accessibility/copy reviews, provenance, version/withdrawal fields, quotas, and non-copying expression evidence.\n\nDo not author product code, implementation B/R runbooks, copied questions or reference-product expression. This task does not accept the manifest.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The finite 48-card first-release catalogue is bounded, original, and independently quota/provenance verifiable.\n### game-design-runbooks/G0002.md\n---\ntask_id: G0002\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: G0001\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,planning/game-production-inventory.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-003,GAME-004,GPI-006,GPI-007\ntitle: Define fair adjudication and editorial lifecycle bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0001\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-003\u2013004/GPI-006\u2013007: documented normalisation/alias policy, 20 fair adjudication fixtures, withdrawal states, and seeded anti-repeat/shortage policy.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md`: deterministic select/true-false/ordered/typed-answer rules, 20 fixtures, contested-fact withdrawal/provenance review states, and a seeded anti-repeat/shortage rule.\n\nNo fuzzy guessing, implementation code, B/R runbooks, or manifest acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Rules never guess answers and every catalogue-state transition is reproducible.\n### game-design-runbooks/G0003.md\n---\ntask_id: G0003\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: GB0002,G0002\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-005,GAME-006,GPI-008,GPI-009\ntitle: Define tutorial and standard-round bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0002\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-005\u2013006/GPI-008\u2013009: TUT-01\u201305, mixed 10-card round selection, optional timer, offline lifecycle, interruption and shortage behaviour.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md`: named First Whistle cards and transitions, Mixed Fixture selection/shortage fixtures, optional-off timer, offline pause/resume lifecycle, and accessibility review.\n\nDo not invent a campaign, live/ranked mode, code, B/R runbooks, or manifest acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every named tutorial card and round transition has a deterministic fixture.\n### game-design-runbooks/G0004.md\n---\ntask_id: G0004\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: G0003\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,planning/game-production-inventory.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-007,GAME-008,GPI-010,GPI-011\ntitle: Define scoring and results bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0002\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-007\u2013008/GPI-010\u2013011: 100-point capped-streak table, feedback equivalents, result states, milestone idempotence, and 18 edge/lifecycle fixtures.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md`: score/streak rule table, 18 recovery/result fixtures, idempotent milestones, and text, non-colour, captioned/mute audio-equivalent feedback requirements.\n\nDo not create implementation code or B/R runbooks, and do not accept the manifest.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Wrong, blank, timeout, and abandon remain recoverable and do not create duplicate completion.\n### game-design-runbooks/G0005.md\n---\ntask_id: G0005\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: GB0003,G0004\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-009,GAME-010,GAME-011,GAME-012,GPI-012,GPI-013,GPI-014,GPI-015\ntitle: Define accessible recovery and target parity bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0003\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-009\u2013012/GPI-012\u2013015: four input mappings, captions/contrast/text/motion equivalents, four recovery states, offline/update notices, and web/PWA/Android/iOS parity and certification matrix.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md`: four input mappings, accessible feedback equivalents, recovery/offline/update states, and web/PWA/Android/iOS rule/content/save parity matrix.\n\nDo not create target-exclusive content, mandatory accounts/sync, code, B/R runbooks, or manifest acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Each meaning has a non-audio, non-colour equivalent and target adaptations cannot alter shared rules or saves.\n### game-design-runbooks/GD0001.md\n---\ntask_id: GD0001\nsequence: 1\ndependencies:\nsource_specifications: specification/00-domain-discovery.md,specification/01-game-identity.md,specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/02-game-design-bible.json,specification/01-creative-direction.md,planning/game-production-inventory.md,planning/game-production-inventory.json\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GAME-003,GAME-004,GAME-005,GAME-006,GAME-007,GAME-008,GAME-009,GAME-010,GAME-011,GAME-012,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005,GPI-006,GPI-007,GPI-008,GPI-009,GPI-010,GPI-011,GPI-012,GPI-013,GPI-014,GPI-015\ntitle: Dispatch bounded football-trivia game-design programme\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nRead `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../INITIAL.md`, `../specification/00-domain-discovery.md`,\n`../specification/01-game-identity.md`, `../specification/02-game-design-bible.{md,json}`,\n`../specification/01-creative-direction.md`, and\n`../planning/game-production-inventory.{md,json}`. Maintain\n`../planning/game-design-manifest.json` as the completion gate; it starts\npending and must not be marked accepted by this dispatcher.\n\nCreate no more than three bounded GB writers, one per selected module, plus\n`GC0001.md`. Register each new file's normal Supervisor metadata and output\npaths. Each GB writer may create at most five focused `G####.md` tasks, and\nevery G task must declare its actual `design_authoring_batch: GB####`.\n\nFor this football-trivia programme, allocate design evidence for: original\nquestion-card grammar and four named QB-A editorial batches with sources and\nreviews; adjudication/fairness and anti-repeat rules; First Whistle, Mixed\nFixture, score/streak/results rules; guided accessibility, recovery/offline,\nand target parity. G tasks must create/review detailed bibles, not code and not\nimplementation B/R runbooks.\n\n`GC0001` must check G ownership, the five-G-per-GB limit, canonical GAME and\nGPI coverage, dependency closure, original-expression/provenance evidence,\nasset/audio accessibility equivalents, output quality, and manifest\nconsistency. If any selected module or production entry lacks accepted detailed\nevidence, create exactly one successor `GD####` dispatcher for the next bounded\nwave. When all required evidence is accepted