ional team | FIFA |\n151:| QB-A-39 | OP | 1 | Order Lionel Messi's 2009 and 2010 Ballon d'Or wins \u2014 2009, 2010 | Ballon d'Or | FF |\n152:| QB-A-40 | TA | 1 | Premier League all-time top scorer (as official record) \u2014 Alan Shearer | Premier League | PL |\n153:| QB-A-41 | FO | 2 | 2018 FIFA World Cup Golden Ball winner \u2014 Luka Modri\u0107 | FIFA World Cup | FIFA |\n154:| QB-A-42 | TF | 2 | Lionel Messi won The Best FIFA Men's Player award for 2022 \u2014 true | The Best FIFA Football Awards | FIFA |\n155:| QB-A-43 | OP | 2 | Order Mohamed Salah's Premier League Golden Boots in 2018 and 2019 \u2014 2018, 2019 | Premier League | PL |\n156:| QB-A-44 | TA | 2 | 2019\u201320 Premier League Golden Boot co-winner \u2014 Pierre-Emerick Aubameyang | Premier League | PL |\n157:| QB-A-45 | FO | 3 | 2006 FIFA World Cup Golden Boot winner \u2014 Miroslav Klose | FIFA World Cup | FIFA |\n158:| QB-A-46 | TF | 3 | Robert Lewandowski won The Best FIFA Men's Player award for 2020 \u2014 true | The Best FIFA Football Awards | FIFA |\n159:| QB-A-47 | OP | 3 | Order the 2018 and 2019 Ballon d'Or winners \u2014 Luka Modri\u0107, Lionel Messi | Ballon d'Or | FF |\n160:| QB-A-48 | TA | 3 | Premier League single-season goal record holder (38-match season) \u2014 Erling Haaland | Premier League | PL |\n162:## Mechanical release checks\n165:from published card records and their provenance/review records:\n169:| ID/boundary | Exactly 48 unique IDs, exactly `QB-A-01\u202648`, exactly four named batches of 12; no extra QB-A card. |\n175:| Eligibility | Every card is `published`, has all grammar fields, a resolvable provenance record with a checked date, no unresolved conflict, two distinct accepted reviews of its current revision, and no withdrawal. |\n176:| Originality/accessibility | Every card has accepted originality and accessibility/copy review findings, required text equivalents, and no player-facing copied/source text. |\n179:review are completed. Thus it is bounded and independently auditable now, while\n181:provenance and both reviews are supplied.\n## design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md\n1:# Round lifecycle bible\n3:**Scope:** accepted design evidence for `GAME-005`, `GAME-006`, `GPI-008`, and\n4:`GPI-009`. This defines a future-core contract and fixtures, not production\n9:## GPI-008 \u2014 First Whistle tutorial\n15:published wording, answer IDs, provenance, and two reviews are governed by the\n21:| 2 / `TUT-02` | short typed answer | Enter a short answer and confirm; only configured canonical text/aliases are accepted. | A typed submission resolves through GAME-003 normalisation, shows canonical answer/explanation if rejected, and opens `TUT-03`. |\n32:### Tutorial deterministic fixtures\n36:GAME-003 fixture supplies an immutable accepted/rejected attempt; the\n42:| `TUT-FX-02` | From TUT-02 submit a configured typed alias, resolve, continue. | `TUT-02 \u2192 TUT-03`; outcome is the configured GAME-003 alias result and is not recomputed on continue. |\n50:## GPI-009 \u2014 Mixed Fixture selection\n55:GAME-004 frozen-catalogue, publication, withdrawal, filter, anti-repeat, and\n71:### Seeded Mixed Fixture fixtures\n74:from the stated frozen snapshot and seed under GAME-004. Each token is\n88:## Optional timer and round lifecycle\n95:enabled timer according to the separately implemented GAME-007 scoring rule.\n109:### Lifecycle deterministic fixtures\n127:## Accessibility and release boundary\n140:answer rules remain subject to the editorial/provenance validation contracts.\n## design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md\n1:# Score, streak, and results bible\n3:**Scope:** accepted design evidence for `GAME-007`, `GAME-008`, `GPI-010`, and\n4:`GPI-011`. This is a deterministic future-core contract, not implementation or\n5:production content. It consumes immutable `GAME-003` adjudication outcomes and\n6:the frozen run/card sequence from `GPI-009`. A run ID, attempt ID, interaction\n11:## GPI-010 \u2014 score and streak contract\n47:### Equivalent feedback requirements\n66:### Score and feedback edge fixtures\n87:## GPI-011 \u2014 results and local milestone contract\n89:### Result states\n105:### Completion and milestone idempotence\n118:their own immutable history/result once, but cannot replace those provenance\n122:### Result and lifecycle fixtures\n133:## Release boundary\n=== canonical ids ===\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:11:| GAME-001 | GPI-001: one card schema, five format fixtures | \u2014 | Editorial + tooling | Schema/negative fixtures |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:12:| GAME-002 | GPI-002\u2013005: four named 12-card batches, QB-A-01\u201348 | GPI-001 | Editorial + two reviewers | Provenance, review, quota, uniqueness validator |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:13:| GAME-003 | GPI-006: four handlers, 20 adjudication fixtures | GPI-001 | Rules + core | Deterministic acceptance/rejection fixtures |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:14:| GAME-004 | GPI-007: selection policy, 8 seeded fixtures | GPI-002\u2013005 | Editorial + core | Repeat/shortage/withdrawal tests |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:15:| GAME-005 | GPI-008: TUT-01\u201305 fixed tutorial | GPI-001, 006, 013\u2013014 | Design + editorial | Offline completion/resume test |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:16:| GAME-006 | GPI-009: one 10-card Mixed Fixture template | GPI-002\u2013007 | Rules + core | Seeded selection lifecycle |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:17:| GAME-007 | GPI-010: rule table, 12 edge fixtures | GPI-006, 009 | Rules + accessibility | Score/streak equivalent-feedback tests |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:18:| GAME-008 | GPI-011: result and milestone states | GPI-009\u2013010, 014 | Design + UI | Idempotence/recovery lifecycle tests |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:19:| GAME-009 | GPI-012: profile/settings plus four input maps | \u2014 | Accessibility + platform | Input and accessibility review |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:20:| GAME-010 | GPI-013: four recovery states, eight faults | GPI-011 | Persistence + accessibility | Fault-injection recovery tests |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:21:| GAME-011 | GPI-014: cache/update notices and six fixtures | GPI-002\u2013005, 013 | Release + platform | Offline/update/error tests |\nplanning/game-production-inventory.md:22:| GAME-012 | GPI-015: four-target parity/certification matrix | GPI-012\u2013014 | Platform + release | Target evidence and certification checklist |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:18:### Quiz content and editorial integrity \u2014 `GAME-001` to `GAME-004`\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:27:| GAME-001 | **Question-card grammar.** An original card has one unambiguous fact, prompt, format, category, era/competition tags, difficulty 1\u20133, answer rule, short explanation, and review/version state. Formats: four-option select, true/false, ordered pair, and short typed answer. | Ship only reviewed `published` cards. A card without provenance, answer rule, explanation, or two-editor approval is ineligible. Test: each sampled card adjudicates its canonical and configured accepted answers identically. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:28:| GAME-002 | **Catalogue batch A: \u201cKickoff Mix.\u201d** 48 original cards: 12 world tournament history, 12 domestic league moments, 12 club/manager/identity, 12 players/records. Each category has 4 cards at each band, max 6 cards per competition and no single club above 4. | Finite named release package: `QB-A-01` through `QB-A-48`, authored in four 12-card editorial batches. Exact facts, wording, sources, and rights clearance remain an editorial approval gate; placeholders never ship. Test: the manifest enforces totals, distributions, unique IDs, and no unpublished card. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:29:| GAME-003 | **Adjudication and provenance.** Select/true-false compare canonical IDs. Ordered pair compares ordered IDs. Typed answers normalise Unicode, case, punctuation, whitespace, diacritics, and configured aliases; it never uses fuzzy matching in release one. A rejected typed answer shows the canonical answer and explanation. | Each factual assertion links to a durable permitted source or approved internal research note, with checked date, reviewer, and correction history. Conflict or contested fact \u21d2 remove from eligibility until resolved. Test: alias, malformed, blank, ambiguous, and outdated-version cases have fixtures. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:30:| GAME-004 | **Freshness.** The repeat ledger records card ID and completion timestamp locally. A round excludes cards seen in its last two completed rounds where alternatives exist; if insufficient eligible cards exist, it discloses reuse rather than silently failing. | No renewable feed, scraping, or live refresh. Authoring flow: propose \u2192 source/provenance \u2192 factual check \u2192 accessibility/copy edit \u2192 second review \u2192 publish to a versioned batch \u2192 validate \u2192 release/rollback. Test: seeded selection is reproducible and respects the exclusion rule. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:39:### Round, score, and progress rules \u2014 `GAME-005` to `GAME-008`\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:48:| GAME-005 | **Round \u201cFirst Whistle.\u201d** Tutorial round contains 5 fixed, original tutorial cards (`TUT-01`\u2013`TUT-05`) covering selecting, typing, feedback, explanation, and pause/save. It is intentionally non-timed. | This is the complete first useful journey. Completion creates/updates local milestone `first_whistle_complete`; it cannot require account, network, purchase, or deferred content. Test: a new local profile can complete it offline and resume after app restart. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:49:| GAME-006 | **Round \u201cMixed Fixture.\u201d** A 10-card themed round draws from one selected category or the Kickoff Mix, with no more than two adjacent cards sharing format or difficulty. The player may pause; a displayed timer mode is optional and defaults off. | First release ships one tutorial and one configurable standard round template, no ranked/daily/live/event modes. Test: deterministic seed produces ten eligible cards and valid format alternation or records the shortage. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:50:| GAME-007 | **Scoring and streak.** Correct = 100 points; a consecutive-correct streak of 3+ adds 25 points to each later correct answer, capped at +100. Incorrect, timeout (only if enabled), blank submission, or abandon resets the active streak; score never decreases. Explanation is available after resolution. | No paid boosts, leaderboard, social comparison, or opaque difficulty multiplier. Test: table-driven sequence proves cap, reset, and per-attempt result; a retry is a new run, not an overwrite of history. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:51:| GAME-008 | **Result and return.** Results show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, and next action: replay, choose theme, or exit. Progress is local milestones and aggregate history only, not RPG levels. | An interrupted run persists at a safe boundary before the next unresolved question. Completed result is idempotent: reopening cannot award twice. Test: complete/reopen, abandon/resume, corrupted draft, and delete-history paths are specified. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:53:**Dependencies:** GAME-005 needs published tutorial cards and persistence;\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:54:GAME-006 needs GAME-001\u2013004; GAME-007 consumes adjudication events; GAME-008\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:59:### Accessible, recoverable multi-target experience \u2014 `GAME-009` to `GAME-012`\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:68:| GAME-009 | **Guided start.** First launch offers an accessible plain-language tutorial entry, settings access, and a local profile without sign-in. Controls map select/navigate/confirm/back/pause to touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad. | No mandatory account. Permission denial for optional notifications/diagnostics changes no game path and explains how to alter it later. Test: every critical action is operable with keyboard and touch, focus is visible, and gamepad has an equivalent mapping. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:69:| GAME-010 | **Save/recovery.** Save immutable confirmed snapshots at tutorial completion, resolved question boundaries, explicit pause, and completed results. On failed write, retain the last confirmed snapshot and show retry/continue-without-saving. On corrupt draft, offer last confirmed snapshot or discard draft; never silently overwrite. | Remote sync/conflict requires approval and is excluded. Local deletion requires confirmation, names its effect, clears local profile/history/snapshots, and returns to first launch. Test: write failure, crash/restart, corrupt draft, and deletion fixtures preserve stated invariants. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:70:| GAME-011 | **Offline/update/error.** The installed content batch and current snapshot remain playable offline. A new content version is staged between rounds; an incompatible cache reports recovery steps and preserves confirmed save before cache reset. Unexpected errors show a plain-language retry/return-home path and optional minimised diagnostic consent. | No background live content requirement. Test: offline launch with cached assets, update mid-round, unavailable content, and diagnostic permission-denied behaviours are covered. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:71:| GAME-012 | **Platform adaptation.** Shared rule/content/save semantics on responsive web, PWA, Android, and iOS. Web adds pointer/keyboard/gamepad and responsive layouts; PWA adds install/offline cache/update UX; phones add touch targets and approved portrait/landscape choice. | No target-exclusive questions or rule differences. OS/browser matrix, orientation, performance, battery, thermal, size, store/privacy declarations, crash vendor, and exact language set remain approval gates. Test: capability matrix is exercised once targets are chosen. |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:93:| GAME-001\u2013004 | J1/J2/J4 (and J5 for versioned batch) | B content/adjudication; F delivery for batch lifecycle |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:94:| GAME-005\u2013008 | J1/J2/J3 | A shell/progress; C rules/score/feedback; D persistence for return |\nspecification/02-game-design-bible.md:95:| GAME-009\u2013012 | J0/J1/J2/J3/J5 | D recovery, E accessibility/input/presentation, F delivery/targets |\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The ownership, caps, canonical ID coverage, and dependency references are coherent. The gate is not complete: every QB-A card remains explicitly `draft` with only pending review records, so the required source/provenance and two accepted reviews do not yet exist. I\u2019m recording that checkpoint and creating the single bounded successor rather than accepting the manifest.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GD0002.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-design-manifest.json\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GD0002.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GD0002.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..86fc67999619585b930605d5f6bb6e6ad6bf39ec\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GD0002.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@\n+---\n+task_id: GD0002\n+sequence: 5\n+dependencies: GC0001\n+source_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/02-game-design-bible.json,planning/game-production-inventory.md,planning/game-production-inventory.json,planning/game-design-manifest.json,design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md,design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md\n+source_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GAME-003,GAME-004,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005,GPI-006,GPI-007\n+title: Complete QB-A editorial acceptance evidence\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Close the one incomplete design-evidence boundary found by `GC0001`: the\n+finite QB-A catalogue has a grammar, source policy, quota tables, lifecycle,\n+adjudication, and anti-repeat fixtures, but `QB-A-01` through `QB-A-48` are\n+still `draft` and have only pending reviews. Create or review durable editorial\n+acceptance evidence for the existing four bounded batches only. Do not add\n+cards, change quiz scope, create code/B/R runbooks, or accept the manifest.\n+\n+## Exact pending reasons retained from GC0001\n+\n+- `GPI-001`: the grammar requires a resolvable provenance record and two\n+  distinct accepted current-revision reviews, but it contains no completed\n+  card-level records for `QB-A-01`\u2013`QB-A-48`.\n+- `GPI-002`, `GPI-003`, `GPI-004`, and `GPI-005`: each of the four named\n+  12-card QB-A batches is explicitly recorded as `status: draft`,\n+  `revision: 1`, with `PROV-<ID>` and two pending review records. No card may\n+  become eligible from those placeholders.\n+- `GAME-002`: the required original-expression, factual-source/provenance,\n+  factual/rights review, accessibility/copy review, and independent second\n+  review decisions have not been accepted for any current card revision.\n+- `GAME-004` and `GAME-006` retain their deterministic policy/fixture evidence,\n+  but their use of published catalogue candidates remains co